WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:02.375
The sixth case is zero to the power zero,

2
00:00:02.405 --> 00:00:05.277
in limit calculations. Consider x to the power x

3
00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:07.602
as x approaches zero from the right.

4
00:00:07.696 --> 00:00:10.396
Both base and exponent approach zero.

5
00:00:10.574 --> 00:00:12.614
Call x to the power x

6
00:00:12.665 --> 00:00:16.676
y. Take logarithms to obtain ln y equal to

7
00:00:16.676 --> 00:00:18.269
x multiplied by ln x.

8
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.491
We have already seen that x times ln x

9
00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:23.358
tends to zero as x approaches zero

10
00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:26.208
from the right. Thus ln y tends to zero.

11
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.085
Apply the exponential function. y tends to e to the power zero,

12
00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:32.176
which is one. Therefore the limit

13
00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:33.598
of x to the power x here is one.

14
00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:35.240
This is the result of this limit,

15
00:00:35.291 --> 00:00:37.509
not a general definition of zero to the power zero.
